#
# Jumbo frames through the coprocessor's switch chip, at every boot - scripts/xgs/switch-jumbo.sh.
#
# A start hook, so it runs once the boot is done and the coprocessor's own setup of the switch is
# over; detached, because the first boot after an install puts the switch tool on the coprocessor,
# which over the XGS 3300's console takes about three minutes, and a boot must not wait for that.
# The script logs what it found and did (tag xgs-switch) and never fails the boot.
SCRIPT=/usr/local/opnsense/scripts/xgs/switch-jumbo.sh
[ -f "${SCRIPT}" ] || exit 0
/usr/sbin/daemon -f /bin/sh "${SCRIPT}"
exit 0
